The 32-bit setjmp source and machine headers are declared target inputs.
The original filesystem size policy applies only to the ffs_subr compiler;
existing per-source cryptographic assertion policy is retained.
Private EFI objects use separate compiler contexts and explicit verifier inputs.
These internal archives do not add installed userland libraries.
Complete BIOS and IA32 loader programs require further qualification.
.Ss IA32 interpreter archives
The liblua32 and ficl32 components and their private EFI variants use the shared
