EFI objects retain short wchar and double alignment independently of regular
BIOS objects.  The IA32 EFI Lua Make wrapper shares the native-width private
verification policy, including authenticated-source checks.
Host tests inspect ELF32 member order, interpreter APIs and verifier isolation;
compile-time Lua checks cover its number, FILE and EFI wchar ABI.
These archives remain internal.  Complete IA32 loader boot execution and full
debug parity require separate qualification.
.Ss Complete IA32 EFI Lua construction
The loader_ia32 contribution uses explicit i386 startup sources, target headers,
link script and private libraries in the shared loader graph.
Its installation manifest contributes only /boot/loader_ia32.efi: it creates
neither the native-width default-loader link nor another shared help file.
The image converter selects PE32 for IA32; an EFI subsystem does not imply
PE32+.  Host artifact tests verify the real firmware header, linked symbols
and installation policy against the selected timestamp setting.
These checks do not execute firmware or establish verified boot.
.Ss BIOS platform support archive
The source-owned stand/i386/libi386 archive uses the explicit i386 standalone
