The loader_gptboot_ufs setting accepts UFS1_AND_UFS2, UFS1_ONLY or UFS2_ONLY.
The loader_isoboot_max_size integer setting defaults to Make's 30720-byte bound;
the real completed image must pass that bound before becoming the public artifact.
Both components provide installation manifests and archives with original image
and manual policy. The shared boot-data rules honor the existing man, mancompress
and split_manpages settings. Construction tests and original compiler controls do not
qualify firmware execution, full-system debug lookup or system performance.
.Ss GPT/ZFS BIOS boot construction
The gptzfsboot contribution uses ten original standalone i386 compiler contexts,
