Package creation tests still require an explicit package_version setting;
qualification versions do not publish or install an upgrade.
Complete usr.bin/LLVM family aggregation and installed-world coverage remain open.

.Ss LLVM family composition under qualification
The normal installed LLVM family is being composed through the existing
format-5 interface. The clang setting controls compiler selection separately
from clang_full feature selection. CLANG_EXTRAS and complete installed-world
coverage remain open. The usr.bin test-root contribution uses the maintained
source Kyuafile, which discovers installed child test directories.
No new C dispatcher or publication interface is required for these declarations;
configured ownership and strict merged-manifest analysis pass. The subsequent
AMD64 production aggregate and six selected configuration/runtime tests pass;
complete world installation and other profiles remain open.
The seven archive contributions account for 17 default Make directories because
the toolchain contribution closes ten utility manifests and their manual links.
This is a configuration checkpoint, not full-system acceptance.

.Ss usr.bin production family under qualification
The explicit format-5 interface can select
.Cm //usr.bin:production_installation_archives
for the configured AMD64 production contributions.
Configured ownership matches the retained Make profile. Native aggregate
compilation and archive production pass with six selected tests; independent
full Make installation parity and complete world qualification remain open.
A separate audit verifies all 267 captured archives against requests and logged
payloads: 1,482 file/link paths, no duplicate non-directory destinations.
Thirteen cached outputs are bound to matching prior actual producer records,
not reported as fresh executions.
.Cm //usr.bin:installation_archives
rejects tests-enabled configurations until the complete original installed
test hierarchy is reconciled. The production target does not assert test coverage.
The unconverted Heimdal compiler profile
is explicitly incompatible; its conversion remains required work.
These targets add no publication, installation or upgrade authorization.

.Ss Test-root shared metadata export
The generic Kyuafile source is available to the usr.bin subtree through the same
restricted export used by bin/sbin/libexec. The initial missing export is retained
as failed qualification evidence. Corrected native qualification passes and
its actual archive matches the original Make files, ownership, modes, directory
and package tags. This does not establish complete child test installation. The format-5 dispatch and publication interface remain unchanged.

.Ss Original TAP suite archives under qualification
The existing format-5 inputs can select the install_archive targets beneath
usr.bin's apply, calendar, comm, file2c, join, jot, lastcomm, ncal, printf, tr and
units tests directories. Shared native helpers preserve original TAP scripts,
fixtures and Kyua metadata. Native archive qualification and exact Make
installation comparison pass for 283 files and eleven explicit directories,
including payload bytes, modes, ownership and tags. Archive construction
does not execute those TAP programs or close the full installed-test inventory.
No dispatch, staging-policy, signing or publication interface change is required.

.Ss Captured artifact batch inspection
The maintained qualification artifact reader supports nonempty batches selected
by explicit target and output suffix. It parses a verified receipt and manifest
once, validates every selected payload's containment, size and SHA-256, and
rechecks metadata before returning. Ambiguous selections, corrupted payloads
and metadata changes are rejected. The single-output interface uses the same
checks. This changes inspection metadata I/O, not build caching, signing,
publication policy or the format-5 dispatcher.

.Ss Optional Hesiod consumer
The existing format-5 hesiod setting selects the AMD64 hesinfo archive through
the usr.bin parent. The program links configured native libc and uses its source
Hesiod header. Native archive construction and safe usage testing pass; an
independent original reference needs a coherent HESIOD-enabled SDK, and full
DNS runtime qualification remains open. Disabled Hesiod excludes the contribution.
Existing file2c native tests use explicit test-package fixture labels with
restricted parent exports; no fixture bytes or installed metadata are changed.

The corrected full production aggregate and all nine existing native file2c
cases pass; its 801 captured archive/request/directory outputs match the previous
passing aggregate. Configured Hesiod parent queries preserve the disabled set
and add only the Hesiod contribution when enabled. These are bounded component
checks, not complete world, package or DNS service acceptance.

