Source protocol interfaces and the shared native rpcgen header are declared;
configured native libc supplies optional NIS symbols. The libypclnt shared link
also declares that native libc/libsys dependency instead of assuming SDK exports.
Four consumer object contracts match fresh Make objects; archive serialization
and safe alias-list tests pass. Complete linked/staged client parity, live RPC,
authentication and full-system qualification remain open.

The complete combined NIS/Hesiod production profile passes with 271 archives and
four selected tests. NIS-enabled quota/chpass links also select configured native
libc. Library links use the DSO interface; executable-only nonshared wrappers
remain at executable links. The profile review checks destination uniqueness and
retains the inspected iconv PLT symbol-order difference without claiming byte
parity. No signing, publication or host installation policy changes are added.

The separate final default-profile regression passes, with all 801 production
archive/request/directory outputs unchanged from the previous default capture.

.Ss Private implementation dependency qualification
The existing format-5 native workflow supports libsys's private bcopy.c include
