memcpy variants and no longer propagates into NIS consumer compile inputs.
Four actual compiler commands and object bytes, nine archive products and both
native libc/libsys shared-library bytes remain unchanged. Six selected tests
pass: three runtime cases execute and three previous results are cached.
This verifies an inspected dependency boundary; complete mutation, cache-restore,
sandbox and comparative resource qualification remain required.
No frontend C, signing or publication policy change is needed.

An unchanged repeat preserves all 22 selected output records with zero actual
logged spawn actions and six cached test results. This is local up-to-date
reuse in maintained persistent state, not cold-build or cache-restore proof.

