Selected original installation, ELF dependency/interface/hardening and debug CRC
comparisons pass, along with CTF static/shared and standard C++ header tests.
These are scoped construction checks, not daemon runtime or whole-world,
pkgbase, bootstrap, cross-platform or resource acceptance.
The tests and tests_support settings are distinct inputs: disabling installed
tests does not require disabling Kyua when tests_support is explicitly enabled.
Generic label and setting dispatch requires no new C selector.
Make remains the default; signing and publication requirements are unchanged.

The follow-up library batch builds the CTF-enabled libproc branch and passes
nine CTF/SPL/AVL/nvpair tests. Nvpair preserves the original SPL-before-RPC
