.Pp
The MIT Kerberos production-products endpoint includes its installed archives
and both original variants of all five internal libraries.
Internal profile and command libraries produce build outputs without installed
headers or scripts, following the maintained Make install rules.
PIE program consumers select the profile PIE variant, matching original Make
links.
Selected local crypto, principal, GSS, profile and utility tests do not establish
KDC service, network authentication or credential-lifecycle acceptance.

.Pp
Native share-data targets preserve the installed Make support files required by
ports, repository trust-key payloads, skeleton-file permissions, dictionary links
and selected USB/editor data.
These component targets do not yet constitute a complete share or world endpoint.

