The native ordinary public header endpoint uses source-owned lists and selects
iconv, Hesiod and legacy GSS headers from configured source options.
Disabling includes also disables optional header contributions.
This endpoint is separate from generated version headers, kernel header groups
and compatibility aliases; it does not establish complete include/world parity.

